WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.541


2
00:00:33.541 --> 00:00:36.500
<b>On the sacred land of Kurukshetra, </b>

3
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.166
<b>the war could begin at any moment. </b>

4
00:00:39.166 --> 00:00:40.833
<b>Just a short while ago</b>

5
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:43.375
<b>Dhritarashtra had asked Sanjaya,</b>

6
00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:44.916
<b>"O Sanjaya,</b>

7
00:00:44.916 --> 00:00:47.208
<b>having gathered on the dharma-kshetra,</b>
<b>the field of Kurukshetra, </b>

8
00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:52.916
<b>what are my sons and the sons of Pandu</b>
<b>doing, eager for battle?"</b>

9
00:00:52.916 --> 00:00:53.458
<b>Now, </b>

10
00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:59.541
<b>in this verse, Sanjaya begins to answer </b>
<b>that very question posed by Dhritarashtra. </b>

11
00:00:59.541 --> 00:01:00.791
<b>He narrates </b>

12
00:01:00.791 --> 00:01:02.250
<b>how King Duryodhana,</b>

13
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.791
<b>upon seeing the military formation of the </b>
<b>Pandava army, </b>

14
00:01:04.791 --> 00:01:08.458
<b>first approached his teacher Dronacharya. </b>

15
00:01:08.458 --> 00:01:10.625
<b>What Duryodhana said next </b>

16
00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:13.750
<b>is described in the following verses. </b>

17
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:17.250
<b>Sanjaya knows well in his heart that this</b>

18
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.333
<b>battle of Mahabharata</b>

19
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:23.291
<b>is a war between dharma and adharma, </b>
<b>truth and untruth. </b>

20
00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:24.708
<b>He also knows </b>

21
00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:28.416
<b>that this time, the Kauravas stand </b>
<b>in the grip of adharma,</b>

22
00:01:28.416 --> 00:01:31.666
<b>while the Pandavas are </b>
<b>under the shelter of dharma. </b>

23
00:01:31.666 --> 00:01:38.416
<b>It's not that Sanjaya never advised his </b>
<b>king Dhritarashtra on this matter before. </b>

24
00:01:38.416 --> 00:01:39.541
<b>But </b>

25
00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:41.583
<b>that time has passed.</b>

26
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:44.750
<b>And here lies Sanjaya's sense of duty </b>

27
00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.791
<b>even knowing all this,</b>

28
00:01:46.791 --> 00:01:49.833
<b>he will fulfill his responsibility towards his </b>
<b>king Dhritarashtra. </b>

29
00:01:49.833 --> 00:01:51.375
<b>He will fulfill the duty </b>

30
00:01:51.375 --> 00:01:52.458
<b>He will fulfill the duty </b>

31
00:01:52.458 --> 00:01:56.958
<b>of being the narrator of the Mahabharata.</b>

32
00:01:57.541 --> 00:02:01.750


33
00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:06.750
<b>Seeing the vastness of the Pandava army </b>
<b>Duryodhana is worried.</b>

34
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.541
<b>But </b>

35
00:02:07.541 --> 00:02:10.000
<b>he cannot express this worry.</b>

36
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.791
<b>The commander of the Kaurava army, </b>
<b>Grandsire Bhishma,</b>

37
00:02:12.791 --> 00:02:14.458
<b>is present right there, </b>

38
00:02:14.458 --> 00:02:15.333
<b> yet</b>

39
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:19.666
<b>Duryodhana first approaches </b>
<b>Guru Dronacharya, </b>

40
00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:24.750
<b>and behind this lies a subtle strategy.</b>

41
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.333
<b>Grandsire Bhishma </b>
<b>is committed to Hastinapura. </b>

42
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:33.791
<b>As the commander, he has fully taken </b>
<b>on the responsibility of the Kaurava army, </b>

43
00:02:33.791 --> 00:02:37.666
<b>but he has also taken a vow </b>

44
00:02:37.666 --> 00:02:44.250
<b>that he will not slay any of the five Pandavas.</b>

45
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.125
<b>However, </b>

46
00:02:45.125 --> 00:02:48.958
<b>Guru Dronacharya</b>
<b>is not bound by any such vow, </b>

47
00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:53.750
<b>and among the greatest warriors,</b>
<b>Grandsire Bhishma,</b>

48
00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.250
<b>it is Guru Dronacharya. </b>

49
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.291
<b>He has also been the teacher of the Pandavas </b>

50
00:02:59.291 --> 00:03:04.375
<b>and is well acquainted with their </b>
<b>strengths and weaknesses. </b>

51
00:03:04.375 --> 00:03:05.791
<b>So, by first</b>

52
00:03:05.791 --> 00:03:07.708
<b>going to Guru Drona, </b>

53
00:03:07.708 --> 00:03:10.166
<b>making him feel especially appreciated, </b>

54
00:03:10.166 --> 00:03:15.916
<b>Duryodhana is trying to solidify </b>
<b>Guru Drona's loyalty towards him. </b>

55
00:03:15.916 --> 00:03:23.000
<b>This is Duryodhana's attempt to resolve </b>
<b>the fear rising within his own mind.</b>

56
00:03:23.541 --> 00:03:27.708


57
00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:30.791
<b>The Kaurava army is strong, </b>

58
00:03:30.791 --> 00:03:32.416
<b>immense. </b>

59
00:03:32.416 --> 00:03:34.791
<b>It has the greatest warriors. </b>

60
00:03:34.791 --> 00:03:36.583
<b>There is Grandsire Bhishma,</b>

61
00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.333
<b>there is Guru Drona. </b>

62
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:40.541
<b>Yet, </b>

63
00:03:40.541 --> 00:03:45.125
<b>why is Duryodhana worried? </b>

64
00:03:45.125 --> 00:03:50.583
<b>Why does he need </b>
<b>to resort to such subtle strategy? </b>

65
00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:55.291
<b>The cause of worry lies hidden within the mind, </b>

66
00:03:55.291 --> 00:03:59.250
<b>and this very worry weakens us.</b>

67
00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:03.875
<b>Duryodhana too knows deep down </b>

68
00:04:03.875 --> 00:04:09.125
<b>that he has sided </b>
<b>with deceit and trickery so far. </b>

69
00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:11.083
<b>In such a situation, </b>

70
00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.625
<b>fear and anxiety</b>

71
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:15.500
<b>are but natural, aren't they?</b>

72
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.375
<b>What is true and false, </b>

73
00:04:17.375 --> 00:04:19.250
<b>right and wrong </b>

74
00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.291
<b>our inner conscience knows very well.</b>

75
00:04:22.291 --> 00:04:24.041
<b>It is the human </b>

76
00:04:24.041 --> 00:04:29.541
<b>who blindfolds the mind</b>
<b>with the band of ego and desires. </b>

77
00:04:29.541 --> 00:04:32.041
<b>And then becomes anxious, </b>

78
00:04:32.041 --> 00:04:34.416
<b>tries different ways </b>

79
00:04:34.416 --> 00:04:36.166
<b>to find peace. </b>

80
00:04:36.166 --> 00:04:38.250
<b>Whenever you find yourself in a dilemma, </b>

81
00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.125
<b>or worried,</b>

82
00:04:40.125 --> 00:04:42.916
<b> just look within. </b>

83
00:04:42.916 --> 00:04:45.000
<b>Both will be visible. </b>

84
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.333
<b>The truth</b>

85
00:04:46.333 --> 00:04:48.333
<b>and the right path. </b>

86
00:04:48.333 --> 00:04:50.750
<b>This path may be difficult, </b>

87
00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.083
<b>but it is the path</b>

88
00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:53.916
<b>to victory over fear. </b>

89
00:04:53.916 --> 00:04:56.833
<b>The more truth one has in their mind, </b>

90
00:04:56.833 --> 00:05:00.125
<b>the less fear in life.</b>

91
00:05:00.708 --> 00:05:04.875


92
00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:07.833
<b>Duryodhana is worried, </b>

93
00:05:07.833 --> 00:05:10.041
<b>there is a slight fear </b>

94
00:05:10.041 --> 00:05:11.500
<b>that what if </b>

95
00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.166
<b>the outcome of this Mahabharata war</b>

96
00:05:14.166 --> 00:05:18.250
<b>is not in his favour? </b>

97
00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:26.208
<b>then... One reason for Duryodhana going to </b>
<b>Guru Drona first is certainly shrewd diplomacy </b>

98
00:05:26.208 --> 00:05:31.916
<b>but this perspective also cannot be denied, </b>

99
00:05:31.916 --> 00:05:35.208
<b>that at this moment</b>

100
00:05:35.208 --> 00:05:37.791
<b>Duryodhana knows </b>

101
00:05:37.791 --> 00:05:45.375
<b>he is in dire need of both the military experience</b>
<b>and cooperation of his elders.</b>

102
00:05:45.375 --> 00:05:47.458
<b>There are some qualities </b>

103
00:05:47.458 --> 00:05:52.583
<b>that become even more pronounced with age. </b>

104
00:05:52.583 --> 00:05:56.333
<b>Wisdom is paramount among them. </b>

105
00:05:56.333 --> 00:06:01.125
<b>Our elders have far</b>
<b>more life experiences than us. </b>

106
00:06:01.125 --> 00:06:04.291
<b>We may not be able to increase our age, </b>

107
00:06:04.291 --> 00:06:06.291
<b>but</b>

108
00:06:06.291 --> 00:06:08.833
<b>by the guidance of elders</b>

109
00:06:08.833 --> 00:06:15.458
<b>we can certainly gain a part of their wisdom, </b>

110
00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:20.166
<b>we can definitely learn from their experience. </b>

111
00:06:20.166 --> 00:06:23.625
<b>In moments of dilemma,</b>
<b>to consult with an elder,</b>

112
00:06:23.625 --> 00:06:27.666
<b>to respectfully listen</b>
<b>to the experiences they share, </b>

113
00:06:27.666 --> 00:06:32.375
<b>and then to move forward after sifting </b>
<b>through the sieve of one's own discretion, </b>

114
00:06:32.375 --> 00:06:34.541
<b>therein lies prudence.</b>

115
00:06:34.875 --> 00:06:39.125


116
00:06:39.125 --> 00:06:42.458
<b>Duryodhana is a Kshatriya, </b>

117
00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:47.083
<b>and the battlefield is his place of work. </b>

118
00:06:47.083 --> 00:06:49.083
<b>Whatever the reason may have been,</b>

119
00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:52.250
<b>but now that the war is before him, </b>

120
00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:56.166
<b>winning it is his sole objective,</b>

121
00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:59.083
<b>and for this he is doing everything, </b>

122
00:06:59.083 --> 00:07:01.333
<b>and will continue to do so.</b>

123
00:07:01.333 --> 00:07:04.416
<b>He is hiding his worry,</b>

124
00:07:04.416 --> 00:07:09.208
<b>he is suppressing his ego</b>
<b>and honoring his elders, </b>

125
00:07:09.208 --> 00:07:15.083
<b>in the coming times he will also boost</b>
<b>the morale of the warriors standing with him. </b>

126
00:07:15.083 --> 00:07:21.958
<b>If we forget Duryodhana's tainted mind </b>
<b>for a few moments, </b>

127
00:07:21.958 --> 00:07:28.958
<b>we get a major lesson of professional life.</b>

128
00:07:28.958 --> 00:07:33.875
<b>To treat experienced colleagues with respect. </b>

129
00:07:33.875 --> 00:07:37.125
<b>No matter how dire the situation, </b>

130
00:07:37.125 --> 00:07:41.041
<b>to show control over one's fear and anxiety,</b>

131
00:07:41.041 --> 00:07:45.375
<b>to not let it manifest upon one's associates, </b>

132
00:07:45.375 --> 00:07:48.750
<b>this keeps their morale intact. </b>

133
00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:53.083
<b>And this is also the mark of a good leader.</b>

